infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two ways to cut GC overhead — only one has unbounded upside
  compares
    - label Tune or switch the collector
      children
        - label Bounded upside
          desc Shrinks a 200 ms pause to 50 ms — never to zero
        - label Trades one axis for another
          desc ZGC: sub-ms pauses cost ~10–15% throughput and more memory
        - label The work still happens
          desc Same allocation rate — the collector just redistributes it
    - label Reduce allocation pressure
      children
        - label Unbounded upside
          desc Every byte not allocated is GC work that never happens
        - label Moves all three axes together
          desc Pause, throughput, and memory all improve at once
        - label Pays back per request
          desc One saving, repeated across billions of requests
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
